WEBVTT

NOTE Scene 01. Speaker labels and dialogue derive from the original script.
NOTE Time positions aligned using faster-whisper word timestamps; human review still required.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
<v Jack Marlowe>It was a Tuesday night in Manhattan.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:08.040
<v Jack Marlowe>The rain was coming down in buckets, my bank account was emptier than a politician's

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:12.340
<v Jack Marlowe>promises, and my coffee had given up on life sometime around noon.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:18.356
<v Betty>Hey, boss! The landlord called again. Says if we don't pay by Friday, he's changin'

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:19.180
<v Betty>the locks.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.980
<v Jack Marlowe>Tell him I'm investigating the disappearance of our rent money.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.160
<v Betty>I solved that one. Ya spent it!

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.980
<v Jack Marlowe>That's the trouble with having a competent secretary.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.480
<v Betty>That's the trouble with having an incompetent boss.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.921
<v Vivian Cross>Excuse me. Are you Jack Marlow?

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.260
<v Jack Marlowe>Depends who's asking.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.720
<v Betty>If you're collectin' money, he's in Philadelphia.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.860
<v Vivian Cross>My name is Vivian Cross. I understand you're a man who can find things.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.780
<v Jack Marlowe>Depends what you've lost.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.180
<v Vivian Cross>My husband.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.100
<v Jack Marlowe>When did he disappear?

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.300
<v Vivian Cross>Three weeks ago. They found his coat beside the river.

00:00:56.648 --> 00:01:00.580
<v Vivian Cross>No body. The newspapers have practically declared him dead.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.580
<v Betty>Gee, lady. That's a heck of a way to get outta doin' the dishes.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.200
<v Vivian Cross>Yesterday someone broke into his apartment. The only thing missing was his favorite

00:01:11.486 --> 00:01:15.145
<v Vivian Cross>hat. This afternoon I bought it back from a pawnshop.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.600
<v Jack Marlowe>How'd you find it?

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.840
<v Vivian Cross>The pawnbroker knew Ernest. He called me.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.600
<v Vivian Cross>A large, unpleasant man named Knuckles was trying to buy the same hat.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.420
<v Jack Marlowe>Knuckles Malone?

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.100
<v Betty>No relation!

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.480
<v Vivian Cross>I suspect something is hidden inside it.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:36.340
<v Vivian Cross>Ernest was frightened before he disappeared. He wouldn't tell me why.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.220
<v Jack Marlowe>Mind if I take a look?

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.104
<v Vivian Cross>Please do, darling. Two hundred dollars.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.760
<v Vivian Cross>Half now, half when you discover what happened to Ernest.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.760
<v Betty>Congratulations, lady. Ya just bought yourself a detective!

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.300
<v Jack Marlowe>Leave the hat here. Where can I find Knuckles?

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.780
<v Vivian Cross>The Crooked Canary nightclub. And here's the apartment key.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:02.520
<v Vivian Cross>Call me if you discover anything. I'd hate to lose another man this month.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.100
<v Betty>Another man? She met ya thirty seconds ago!

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.200
<v Jack Marlowe>What can I say, Betty? I'm memorable.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.100
<v Betty>So's food poisoning.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:16.600
<v Jack Marlowe>I left the hat with Betty. She had better eyesight, better bookkeeping, and a

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.780
<v Jack Marlowe>considerably lower tolerance for nonsense.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.920
<v Betty>I'll check the hat while you're out. Try not to come back with any extra holes

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:24.420
<v Betty>in ya.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.640
<v Jack Marlowe>I had two leads.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.860
<v Jack Marlowe>Ernest's apartment might tell me what he was afraid of.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:37.320
<v Jack Marlowe>Or I could visit the Crooked Canary and ask a man built like a refrigerator why

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.500
<v Jack Marlowe>he wanted a secondhand hat.

